# High-level synthesis for the SNAKE chip.
#
# project_vars.sh points qflow at this file with yosys_script, so these lines
# replace the single "synth -top snake_chip" that qflow writes by default.
# Everything around them - reading the liberty file, reading the sources,
# dfflibmap, abc, iopadmap, the final clean - is still qflow's.
#
# The only real change is -flatten before mapping.  The design hands screen
# geometry down as parameters and passes a lot of one bit handshakes between
# blocks, and none of that can be folded across a module boundary.  Flattening
# first lets the constants reach into the sub-blocks: 284 flops instead of 288,
# and about 8% off the combinational cells on its own.
#
# techmap after the first opt is not optional.  "synth -flatten" can leave a
# word level $mux behind, which abc -liberty will not touch and which then
# reaches the placer as an unmapped cell; techmap expands it.  Without this
# line the netlist has exactly one such cell and the flow breaks late.
synth -top snake_chip -flatten
opt -full
techmap
opt -full
